// aug04 fuzz crash_000000 (2026-08-04): SIGABRT in the JIT —
// graphix_valarray_drop asserted on ZERO bits inside a nounwind
// helper. A fold callback whose body is a CONNECT (`|acc, x| a <-
// [..]`) types as Bottom, which unifies with any acc, so the
// signature's tuple acc froze to FoldAcc::Composite — but
// emit_connect_node's value is (NULL|TAINT, 0), a discard-only
// placeholder that violates the owned-composite discipline: the
// drop-replace installed payload 0 as the acc and the next
// iteration's drop_old hit the zero-bits assert. The string-acc twin
// would have been worse (ValArray-shaped 0 as ArcStr bits) — no one
// placeholder serves every acc shape, so the fix is refusal: the
// init/body must THEMSELVES be value-producing shapes (the guard the
// FoldAcc::Value arm already had, jul17a crash_000002, hoisted over
// all acc arms). The interpreted per-slot fold handles the
// never-producing body correctly (fold never fires; both modes
// agree on silence).
{let a = [array::find, i64:0, i64:3]; array::fold([i64:4, i64:5], (i64:1, i64:2), |acc, x| a <- [i64:5, i64:6, i64:7, i64:8])}
